    <div class="post__content post__content--narrow prose">
        <p>Most florists in the UAE start out running their shop on a generic retail till or a spreadsheet, and it works, right up until Valentine’s week. Then the pre-orders pile up, half the stock wilts before it sells, three delivery drivers are calling for addresses, and the till has no idea a rose bouquet contains twelve roses, greenery, and a vase. Flowers are not shelf-stable retail products, and the software that runs a flower shop should not be either.</p>
        <p>Knowing how to choose a flower shop POS comes down to seven practical checks. This guide walks through each one so you can compare vendors with confidence, whether you are replacing an old system or moving off manual billing to a<a href="{{ $base }}/flower-shop-pos-system-in-the-uae/"> POS built for florists</a> for the first time.</p>
        <h2><strong>The 7 Checks at a Glance</strong></h2>
        <figure><table>
